<!--
Enables ClickHouse's native BACKUP/RESTORE. Without a `backups.allowed_disk`
ClickHouse refuses the Disk backup engine outright:

  Code: 318. The 'backups.allowed_disk' configuration parameter is not set,
  cannot use 'Disk' backup engine. (INVALID_CONFIG_PARAMETER)

borgmatic has no ClickHouse hook, so before this the only copy of the
analytics data in the archive was the raw /var/lib/clickhouse directory,
taken while the server was running. That is MergeTree parts plus WAL: not
crash-consistent, and not guaranteed to restore. A borgmatic `commands:
before` hook now writes a real backup here first, mirroring what the four
postgresql_databases hooks already do.

The destination sits INSIDE the event-data volume on purpose. That volume is
already in the borgmatic source set, so the backup gets archived without
changing the backup scope.
-->
<clickhouse>
    <storage_configuration>
        <disks>
            <backups>
                <type>local</type>
                <path>/var/lib/clickhouse/backups/</path>
            </backups>
        </disks>
    </storage_configuration>
    <backups>
        <allowed_disk>backups</allowed_disk>
    </backups>
</clickhouse>
